Id: stor002i
Severity: INFO
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
Fix: Add noexec where nothing needs to run from it.
References: mount(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A world-writable file system (/tmp, /dev/shm, or a separate /var/tmp) is
mounted without noexec, so programs can be run from it directly: a
common step in attacks that download a tool into /tmp and start it.
noexec does not stop a script being run through its interpreter
(sh /tmp/x), so it is a hurdle rather than a wall, and some software
(installers that unpack into /tmp, JIT runtimes using /dev/shm) breaks
with it; that is why this is informational. The CIS benchmarks ask for
it.
